<div class="container">
  <h1 class="h3">JS Parser Tests</h1>
  <p>
    Each test file is loaded twice: from this site and from the original site. Both copies are run and what they
    report is compared. Open this page on a localized domain to test how the proxy translates JavaScript files.
  </p>
  <p>
    The last three files test chunk boundaries inside closing JSON markers. Where the chunks of a response end changes
    from request to request, so run them several times.
  </p>
  <p>
    FAIL means the parser changed what it must not change or broke the file. WARN means a string that may be translated
    came back as it is: usually it is a new string with no translation in the project yet.
  </p>
  <p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="js-tests-run">Run all tests</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" id="js-tests-repeat">Run chunk tests 10 times</button>
    <span id="js-tests-mode" class="ms-2 text-muted"></span>
  </p>
  <div id="js-tests-results"></div>
</div><!-- /.container -->
